From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mali-open
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pan/bi: stop find_all_dominated_predecessors at the fixed point

bi_find_loop_blocks ran |blocks|-1 full CFG sweeps per loop header with no
early exit (17% self time of the whole shaderdb corpus, v13). The set only
grows, so break as soon as a sweep adds nothing; skip blocks already in
the set. Result is bit-identical (shaderdb TSV identical over 290 compiles).
shaderdb compile time, sum over 142 shaders: v11 566 -> 463 ms, v13 559 -> 459 ms (-18%).
---
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
@@ -4661,18 +4661,27 @@
    BITSET_CLEAR_COUNT(out, 0, ctx->num_blocks);
 
    /* If the CFG was one long chain, we would require |blocks|-1 iters to
-    * propagate the in_loop info all the way through.
+    * propagate the in_loop info all the way through. Stop at the fixed point:
+    * most loops converge in a few iterations, so running all |blocks|-1 of
+    * them made this O(blocks^2) per loop header for nothing.
     */
    for (uint32_t iter = 0; iter < ctx->num_blocks - 1; ++iter) {
+      bool progress = false;
       bi_foreach_block(ctx, block) {
+         if (BITSET_TEST(out, block->index) ||
+             !BITSET_TEST(dominators, block->index))
+            continue;
+
          bi_foreach_successor(block, succ) {
-            if ((succ == b || BITSET_TEST(out, succ->index)) &&
-                BITSET_TEST(dominators, block->index)) {
+            if (succ == b || BITSET_TEST(out, succ->index)) {
                BITSET_SET(out, block->index);
+               progress = true;
                break;
             }
          }
       }
+      if (!progress)
+         break;
    }
 }
 
